%   data: {"dataType":"text","outputData":{"text":" <strong>cell<\/strong> - Cell array\n    A cell array is a data type with indexed data containers called cells,\n    where each cell can contain any type of data.\n\n    Creation\n      Syntax\n        C = <strong>cell<\/strong>(n)\n        C = <strong>cell<\/strong>(sz1,...,szN)\n        C = <strong>cell<\/strong>(sz)\n\n        D = <strong>cell<\/strong>(obj)\n\n      Input Arguments\n        <a href=\"matlab:web('C:\\Program Files\\MATLAB\\R2025b\\help\/matlab\/ref\/cell.html#d126e197068')\">n<\/a> - Size of square cell array\n          integer value\n        <a href=\"matlab:web('C:\\Program Files\\MATLAB\\R2025b\\help\/matlab\/ref\/cell.html#d126e197127')\">sz1,...,szN<\/a> - Sizes of dimensions\n          integer values\n        <a href=\"matlab:web('C:\\Program Files\\MATLAB\\R2025b\\help\/matlab\/ref\/cell.html#d126e197190')\">sz<\/a> - Size\n          row vector of integers\n        <a href=\"matlab:web('C:\\Program Files\\MATLAB\\R2025b\\help\/matlab\/ref\/cell.html#d126e197258')\">obj<\/a> - Input array\n          Java array or object |\n          .NET array of type System.String or System.Object |\n          Python sequence type\n\n      Output Arguments\n        <a href=\"matlab:web('C:\\Program Files\\MATLAB\\R2025b\\help\/matlab\/ref\/cell.html#d126e197311')\">C<\/a> - Output array\n          cell array\n        <a href=\"matlab:web('C:\\Program Files\\MATLAB\\R2025b\\help\/matlab\/ref\/cell.html#d126e197331')\">D<\/a> - Converted array\n          cell array\n\n    Object Functions\n      <a href=\"matlab:help cell\/unique -displayBanner\">unique<\/a>    - Unique values\n      <a href=\"matlab:help cell\/setdiff -displayBanner\">setdiff<\/a>   - Difference of two sets of data\n      <a href=\"matlab:help cell\/union -displayBanner\">union<\/a>     - Union of two sets of data\n      <a href=\"matlab:help cell\/intersect -displayBanner\">intersect<\/a> - Intersection of two sets of data\n      <a href=\"matlab:help cell\/ismember -displayBanner\">ismember<\/a>  - Find set members of data\n      <a href=\"matlab:help cell\/setxor -displayBanner\">setxor<\/a>    - Exclusive OR of two sets of data\n      <a href=\"matlab:help cell\/horzcat -displayBanner\">horzcat<\/a>   - Concatenate arrays horizontally\n      <a href=\"matlab:help cell\/vertcat -displayBanner\">vertcat<\/a>   - Concatenate arrays vertically\n\n    Examples\n      <a href=\"matlab:openExample('matlab\/StoreDifferentDataTypesInCellArrayExample')\">Create Cell Array<\/a>\n      <a href=\"matlab:openExample('matlab\/SquareCellArrayExample')\">Square Cell Array<\/a>\n      <a href=\"matlab:openExample('matlab\/DCellArrayExample')\">3-D Cell Array<\/a>\n      <a href=\"matlab:openExample('matlab\/CloneSizeFromExistingArrayExample')\">Clone Size from Existing Array<\/a>\n\n    See also <a href=\"matlab:help num2cell -displayBanner\">num2cell<\/a>, <a href=\"matlab:help table2cell -displayBanner\">table2cell<\/a>, <a href=\"matlab:help iscell -displayBanner\">iscell<\/a>, <a href=\"matlab:help cell2mat -displayBanner\">cell2mat<\/a>, <a href=\"matlab:help cell2struct -displayBanner\">cell2struct<\/a>,\n      <a href=\"matlab:help cell2table -displayBanner\">cell2table<\/a>, <a href=\"matlab:help mat2cell -displayBanner\">mat2cell<\/a>, <a href=\"matlab:help struct2cell -displayBanner\">struct2cell<\/a>\n\n    Introduced in MATLAB before R2006a\n    <a href=\"matlab:doc cell\">Documentation for cell<\/a>\n    <a href=\"matlab:matlab.internal.help.folder.displayList('cell')\">Folders named cell<\/a>\n\n","truncated":false}}
