%[output:2652748c]
%   data: {"dataType":"text","outputData":{"text":" <strong>cellfun<\/strong> - Apply function to each cell in cell array\n    This MATLAB function applies the function func to the contents of each\n    cell of cell array C, one cell at a time.\n\n    Syntax\n      A = <strong>cellfun<\/strong>(func,C)\n      A = <strong>cellfun<\/strong>(func,C1,...,Cn)\n      A = <strong>cellfun<\/strong>(___,Name,Value)\n      [A1,...,Am] = <strong>cellfun<\/strong>(___)\n\n    Input Arguments\n      <a href=\"matlab:web('C:\\Program Files\\MATLAB\\R2025b\\help\/matlab\/ref\/cellfun.html#d126e199330')\">func<\/a> - Function to apply\n        function handle | character vector | string scalar\n      <a href=\"matlab:web('C:\\Program Files\\MATLAB\\R2025b\\help\/matlab\/ref\/cellfun.html#d126e199431')\">C<\/a> - Input array\n        cell array | string array\n\n    Name-Value Arguments\n      <a href=\"matlab:web('C:\\Program Files\\MATLAB\\R2025b\\help\/matlab\/ref\/cellfun.html#d126e199489')\">UniformOutput<\/a> - True or false\n        true (default) | false\n      <a href=\"matlab:web('C:\\Program Files\\MATLAB\\R2025b\\help\/matlab\/ref\/cellfun.html#d126e199561')\">ErrorHandler<\/a> - Function to catch errors\n        function handle\n\n    Output Arguments\n      <a href=\"matlab:web('C:\\Program Files\\MATLAB\\R2025b\\help\/matlab\/ref\/cellfun.html#d126e199628')\">A<\/a> - Output array\n        array of any data type | cell array\n\n    Examples\n      <a href=\"matlab:openExample('matlab\/ApplyFunctionToContentsOfCellArrayExample')\">Apply Function to Contents of Cell Array<\/a>\n      <a href=\"matlab:openExample('matlab\/ApplyFunctionThatAcceptsMultipleInputsExample')\">Return Object Array<\/a>\n      <a href=\"matlab:openExample('matlab\/ReturnMultipleArraysExample')\">Return Multiple Output Arrays<\/a>\n      <a href=\"matlab:openExample('matlab\/ExtractSubstringsFromStringArrayExample')\">Apply Function to Characters in Cell or String Array<\/a>\n\n    See also <a href=\"matlab:help arrayfun -displayBanner\">arrayfun<\/a>, <a href=\"matlab:help spfun -displayBanner\">spfun<\/a>, <a href=\"matlab:help cell2mat -displayBanner\">cell2mat<\/a>, <a href=\"matlab:help structfun -displayBanner\">structfun<\/a>, <a href=\"matlab:help splitapply -displayBanner\">splitapply<\/a>\n\n    Introduced in MATLAB before R2006a\n    <a href=\"matlab:doc cellfun\">Documentation for cellfun<\/a>\n    <a href=\"matlab:matlab.lang.internal.introspective.overloads.displayOverloads('cellfun')\">Other uses of cellfun<\/a>\n\n","truncated":false}}
